cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the preprint below."
title: "uncertainty-vst: benchmarking predictive uncertainty in virtual spatial transcriptomics"
abstract: >-
  Code for "Probabilistic uncertainty in virtual spatial transcriptomics from histology
  is largely redundant with the predicted mean". A systematic benchmark of aleatoric and
  epistemic uncertainty for gene expression predicted from H&E histology on 10x Visium
  spatial transcriptomics, across three cancer cohorts (melanoma, lung, kidney). Compares
  probabilistic likelihood heads (Gaussian, Poisson, negative binomial), deep ensembles,
  MC dropout and last-layer Laplace against histology-free and training-free baselines,
  and scores each predictive distribution for calibration and for error informativeness
  beyond the predicted mean.
